BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kythnos-dryopida-panigiri-of-agioi-anargyroi-at-the-katafyki-cave-dr-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270630
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270702
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agioi Anargyroi at the Katafyki cave\, Dryopida
LOCATION:Dryopida\, Kythnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Kythnos has four Agioi Anargyroi chapels celebrating on 1 July\, but the memorable one is at Dryopida\, where the chapel sits at the mouth of the Katafyki cave that villagers once used as a refuge. Vespers on the evening of 30 June is followed by a glenti with violin and laouto\; it comes two days after the Apostoloi feast\, so a late-June stay in Dryopida catches both.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythnos/#dryopida-panigiri-of-agioi-anargyroi-at-the-katafyki-cave-dr
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythnos/#dryopida-panigiri-of-agioi-anargyroi-at-the-katafyki-cave-dr
END:VEVENT
