DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20280822
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20280824
SUMMARY:Nine-day feast of Panagia Flabouriani\, Flabouria
LOCATION:Flabouria\, Kythnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Named by the municipality among the island's most important feasts: the nine-day of the Dormition at Panagia Flabouriani\, the chapel by the west-coast beach of Flabouria\, on the evening of 22 August and the morning of the 23rd\, with the usual violin-laouto glenti. Panagia Eleousa at Kastro celebrates the same date. The last stretch to Flabouria is a rough track from Chora — a 4x4 or a walk.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythnos/#flabouria-nine-day-feast-of-panagia-flabouriani-flabouria
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythnos/#flabouria-nine-day-feast-of-panagia-flabouriani-flabouria
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kythnos-dryopida-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-prodromos-dryopida-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270830
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Ioannis Prodromos\, Dryopida
LOCATION:Dryopida\, Kythnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The Beheading of St John closes Dryopida's summer: vespers at the Prodromos church on the evening of 28 August and a glenti with the village's violin and laouto players\; the Prodromos in Chora and the chapel of Ai-Giannis tou Skylou celebrate the same night. As it's a strict fast day\, the food is Lenten — expect chickpeas\, olives and fava rather than meat.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythnos/#dryopida-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-prodromos-dryopida
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythnos/#dryopida-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-prodromos-dryopida
END:VEVENT
